  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Standardized Ancestry Feat</strong>: Ancestral Unarmed Attacks</p><hr><p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">The sapien are known for their physical hardiness and immunities, and this is reflected when they use their body to its fullest through training. </span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">When you select this feat, the damage die of your fist unarmed attack changes to 1d6 instead of 1d4. You don’t take the normal -2 circumstance penalty when making a lethal attack with your fist or any other unarmed attacks. Your fist also gains your choice of the trip, grapple, shove or disarm traits.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">At 5th level, whenever you get a critical hit with your unarmed attacks, you get its critical specialization effect.</span></p>"
    },
